# Canonical production AWS SPA configuration.
#
# Do not use `npm run build` / `vite build` for production. That path still
# reads leftover Lovable `.env.production` (Supabase-only) and is rejected by
# `scripts/validate-production-spa-artifact.mjs`.
#
# Required production mechanism from this point forward:
#   node scripts/deploy-production-spa.mjs
# That script builds `--mode production-aws` (this file's values live in
# committed `.env.production-aws`), validates the compiled artifact, and
# records Git commit → SPA bundle → Cognito pool/client → API target → timestamp.
# `--apply` (S3/CloudFront) is refused until the final cutover gate.
#
# - Do not point production at the staging Cognito pool (`us-east-1_vPmQ7cL1F`)
#   or staging API (`psr19uhop4`).
# - Do not put RDS passwords, AWS keys, or provider secrets in any `VITE_*` variable.
# - Step 2 API URL is same-origin `/prep`, not the raw execute-api hostname.
#   `awsApiBaseUrl()` resolves `/prep` against `window.location.origin` so
#   `www.checksops.com` stays same-origin. Do not hardcode `https://checksops.com/prep`.
# - Raw execute-api remains the Step 1–2 rollback URL and must stay enabled:
#   https://kiqojucc02.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/prep
#
# Leftover Lovable `.env.production` remains Supabase-only and must not be
# copied over `.env.production-aws`.

VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER=cognito
VITE_APP_URL=https://checksops.com
VITE_CHECKSOPS_API_URL=/prep
VITE_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_h00WorYMT
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=3ja9fqaq2fjkv3i6up2varcqpe

# CloudFront domain: https://dmgs35lzv89ms.cloudfront.net
# Do not set VITE_APP_URL to the CloudFront domain (WebAuthn RP is checksops.com).

Cognito WebAuthn RP ID must match the production pool (`checksops.com`).
Staging passkeys do not transfer.

Plaid is not required. Leave Plaid disabled on the API.
